==Portuguese==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|pt|tar||colloquial}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|estar}}, from {{inh|pt|la|sto|stāre|t=stand}}, from {{inh|pt|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}. The stems ''estev-'' or ''estiv-'' found in some inflections likely come from {{der|pt|VL.|*stēvī}} (perfect in ''-ēv-'', used by [[:Category:Latin second conjugation verbs with perfect in -ev-|some Latin second conjugation verbs]]), hypothetical perfect stem that displaced original Classical Latin perfect {{m|la|stetī}}. Compare the same development in {{cog|es|estar}}. The present subjunctive stem ''estej-'' is by analogy with {{m|pt|ser}}, ''sej-'' (which is from {{m+|la|sedeo|sedēre}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{pt-IPA}}
* {{audio|pt|LL-Q5146 (por)-D6596-estar.wav|a=Brazil,Rio de Janeiro|IPA=/iʃˈtah/}}
* {{homophones|pt|está|qq1=Brazil}}
* {{hyphenation|pt|es|tar}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb}}

# {{senseid|pt|to be in a place}} {{lb|pt|intransitive}} to [[be]] {{gl|indicates location in space}} {{+obj|pt|:em<location>/another locational preposition or adverb}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Onde '''estás'''?|Where '''are you'''?}}
#: {{uxi|pt|'''Estou''' em casa.|'''I am''' at home.}}
# {{senseid|pt|to be in a transient state}} {{lb|pt|copulative}} to [[be]] {{gl|denotes a [[transient]] quality; a quality expected to change}} {{+obj|pt|adjective}}
#: {{uxi|pt|O tempo '''estava''' frio.|The weather '''was''' cold (''at that moment'').}}
#: {{uxi|pt|'''Estás''' louco?|'''Are''' you crazy (''right now'')?}}
#: {{uxi|pt|A maçã '''está''' madura.|The apple '''is''' ripe.}}
# {{senseid|pt|forms the progressive}} {{lb|pt|auxiliary}} to [[be]]; {{n-g|forms the [[progressive]] aspect}} {{+obj|pt|ger<ll:Brazil>/:a(inf)<ll:Portugal>}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Ela '''está''' cantando? / Ela '''está''' a cantar?|'''Is''' she singing?}}
#: {{uxi|pt|'''Estavam''' trabalhando muito.|'''They were''' working a lot.}}
#: {{uxi|pt|'''Estávamos''' a ler muito.|'''We had been''' reading a lot.}}
#: {{uxi|pt|'''Estaremos''' a ler livros.|'''We will be''' reading books.}}
# {{senseid|pt|to cost}} {{lb|pt|intransitive}} to [[cost]] {{gl|to be worth a certain amount of money}}, especially of something whose price changes often {{+obj|pt|:a<price>}}
#: {{syn|pt|custar}}
#: {{ux|pt|O quilo de maçã '''está''' a dois euros.|t=A kilogram of apples '''costs''' two euros.}}
# {{senseid|pt|to look}} {{lb|pt|copulative}} to [[look]], to [[appear]] {{gl|to give an appearance of being}} {{+obj|pt|adjective}}
#: {{ux|pt|Você '''está''' bonita.|You '''look''' pretty.}}
# to [[stand]]
#: {{ux|pt|Aqui '''estou'''.|Here I '''stand'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* See {{m|pt|ser}}.
* For most speakers the first syllable (''es-'') is usually omited in colloquial language and the full pronunciation is somewhat formal.

