==Spanish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|es|tar||Latin America|nonstandard}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|es|osp|estar}}, inherited from {{inh|es|la|stō|stāre|stand}}, from {{inh|es|ine-pro|*steh₂-}} (compare {{cog|en|stand}}). The preterite's origin is unclear, most likely generalized from the preterite of {{m|es|haber||to have}}, ''hub-'' (note that ''b'' and ''v'' are pronounced identically; compare the same development in {{m|es|andar}} and {{m|es|tener}}). Compare the same development in {{cog|pt|estar}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|state}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr|+<audio:es-us-estar.ogg<a:US>>}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb}}

# {{lb|es|intransitive}} to [[be]] {{gl|have a temporary or permanent location in space}}
#: {{ux|es|¿Dónde '''estás'''?|Where '''are''' you?}}
#: {{ux|es|'''Estoy''' en casa.|I '''am''' at home.}}
# {{lb|es|intransitive}} to [[be]] {{q|denotes a copula, in a [[transient]] fashion}}
#: {{ux|es|El tiempo '''estaba''' frío/caliente.|The weather '''was''' cold/hot [back then].}}
#: {{ux|es|¿'''Estás''' feliz?|'''Are''' you happy [right now]?}}
# to [[be]] {{gl|auxiliary verb for the [[progressive]]/[[continuous]] [[aspect]], preceding the [[gerund]] of the verb}}
#: {{ux|es|Ella '''está''' cantando.|She '''is''' singing.}}
# {{lb|es|intransitive}} to [[be]] in a [[state]] (in a passive voice sense)
#: {{ux|es|Los vasos '''están''' rotos.|The glasses '''are''' broken. (In passive voice with ''estar'', unlike ''haber'', its past participle agrees with number and gender of the subject)}}
#: {{ux|es|Llegaron y vieron que el hotel '''estaba''' abandonado.|They arrived and saw the hotel '''was''' abandoned.}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive|followed by adjective}} to [[be]], [[stay]] {{gl|denotes a copula, in a [[transient]] fashion}}
#: {{ux|es|'''Esten'''se callados y quietos.|'''Stay''' quiet and not moving.}}
# {{lb|es|intransitive}} to [[be]] (still) {{+obj|es|:por(inf)<to be done>}}
#: {{ux|es|Esto todavía '''está''' por hacer.|This is still to be done.}}
#: {{ux|es|Lo peor '''está''' por llegar.|The worst part '''is yet''' to come.}}
# {{lb|es|intransitive}} to [[be]] in a [[long-term]] state {{gl|in specific idioms}}
#: {{ux|es|'''estar''' muerto/a|'''to be''' dead|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|es|'''estar''' casado/a|'''to be''' married (can also be {{m|es||ser casado}})|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|es|'''estar''' chico/a|'''to be''' short (colloquially)|inline=1}}

====Usage notes====
* See {{m|es|ser#Spanish}}. Contrast also with {{m|es|quedar}}.

====Conjugation====
Despite having a vowel in the root, estar's conjugation matches {{m|es|dar}} in the present indicative and present subjunctive tenses, with none of the forms in those tenses being stressed on the root.
